  "read": "Friday closed in extreme fear (11 of 100) after seven down days. Today's +4.8% on Nvidia's board bringing Huang back lifted the number to 28: still fear. Between the lines: the whole gain was the gap. From the 9:30 open the S&P fund finished flat and chips fell 2%, so anyone who waited for the open got nothing and early buyers sold into it. That is relief and short-covering, not fresh buying yet. A VIX of 26.6 and four in five big stocks still under their 20-day average say the crowd has not relaxed.",
  "positioned": "Braced, not bullish. Protection for this month still costs more than protection three months out (1.04), and money moved into health care and utilities during the day. Many who sold last week now hold less than they want, in a market 5% above Friday's close.",
  "surprise": "A slow climb that never gives them the pullback they are waiting for. It would show as SPY holding today's low (713.5) while the VIX slips under its 3-month level. The opposite tell: a close back under 713.5 would say the gap was only short-covering.",
